  "caveats": [
    "\ud83d\uded1 GENERICITY / ANTI-NUMEROLOGY. 'q\u2080 lies between two crossings' is NOT a result: the interval around q\u2080 reproducing the same isotope sign-vector has width 0.1542 = 55.4% of the real-level branch, i.e. only 0.85 bits of constraint, and contains 54 systematically-generated 'natural' constants. q\u2080's position is therefore reported as COINCIDENTAL, not derived. No q was ever solved for to produce a sign pattern (free_parameters=0); the anchor is an input throughout.",
    "CORRECTION TO THE PRIOR A-DEPENDENCE READ. The n=9 crossings previously located at q\u22481.4285/1.4617 lie ABOVE the Wenzl pole q*=1.27845, where the effective level r=log(Q^r)/log(Q) is COMPLEX (r(1.45)=0.81+4.23i) and the principal specialisation s_\u03bb(1,Q,\u2026,Q^{r\u22121}) has no real level. They are therefore NOT comparable to the deuteron crossing at q=1.0537 as members of one monotone trend; this probe sweeps only the real-level branch (1,q*).",
    "Scope-(a) throughout. A LOCATED crossing is a positive existence statement (bracketed sign change of a continuous function). 'No crossing for this n' is a statement about the SWEPT INTERVAL AND GRID only \u2014 a grid can miss an even number of zeros between adjacent points. No invariant is proved to forbid a zero anywhere, so NO scope-(b) exclusion is claimed.",
    "value_only object: F_K and G_n are NOT binding energies (\u0394_\u03bb is value-only, and this probe tests only the SIGN structure of the \u22653-row weighting). The extensive super-pairwise binding MAGNITUDE remains OPEN \u2014 bean qou-prjo is NOT closed.",
    "PRECISION SPLIT. Branch geometry, level ladder and S_n are 50-dps mpmath; the exact-algebraic section is EXACT sympy rational arithmetic with certified VAS/Sturm root isolation (no floating point). \u03c7^\u03bb is f64 (pure-Python Hoefsmit seminormal via the sparse kernel, exact-equal to the dense path to 1.4e-15), so the isotope crossing q values carry f64 resolution only."
  ]
